      "title": "The Brutal Reality of Building Agentic Products Today with Daniel Jeffries - #782",
      "summary": "AI agents are becoming accessible to everyone, raising the bar for developers building the next generation of agent products. When capable, general-purpose agents are available out of the box, differentiation increasingly comes down to the architectural decisions and specialized experiences that make an agent uniquely valuable. In this episode, Dan Jeffries, creator of Nautilo, joins us to discuss what he's learned building a platform for personal and collaborative AI agents. We explore his approach to persistent memory, coordinating work across people and agents, managing private context, and designing deterministic tools that complement LLM capabilities. Dan also shares his views on multi-agent architectures, computer use, and the tradeoffs between local and cloud models. The conversation offers a practitioner's perspective on where the opportunities lie as AI agents become more capable, more accessible, and more difficult to differentiate. \ud83d\uddd2\ufe0f Full show notes: https://twimlai.com/go/782 .",
      "summary_html": "<p>AI agents are becoming accessible to everyone, raising the bar for developers building the next generation of agent products. When capable, general-purpose agents are available out of the box, differentiation increasingly comes down to the architectural decisions and specialized experiences that make an agent uniquely valuable.\n\nIn this episode, Dan Jeffries, creator of Nautilo, joins us to discuss what he's learned building a platform for personal and collaborative AI agents. We explore his approach to persistent memory, coordinating work across people and agents, managing private context, and designing deterministic tools that complement LLM capabilities. Dan also shares his views on multi-agent architectures, computer use, and the tradeoffs between local and cloud models.\n\nThe conversation offers a practitioner's perspective on where the opportunities lie as AI agents become more capable, more accessible, and more difficult to differentiate.\n\n\ud83d\uddd2\ufe0f Full show notes: <a href=\"https://twimlai.com/go/782\">https://twimlai.com/go/782</a>.</p>",
