      "title": "How Security Leaders Are Responding to Machine Speed Threats - with Sridhar Boddula of MassMutual",
      "summary": "The cost and skill required to mount a serious cyberattack have collapsed, and most enterprise security programs still test on a quarterly or annual clock. In this episode, Sridhar Boddula, Head of Security Platform Engineering at MassMutual, breaks down why that mismatch is now the central risk for regulated enterprises and what has to change inside a security team to close it. He covers shifting from periodic testing to continuous validation, moving security from a gatekeeping function into the engineering pipeline, and the governance-first first step leaders should take before scaling any new tooling. This episode is sponsored by XBOW . To learn how leading brands and AI startups connect with enterprise AI buyer audiences at scale, download our media kit at emerj.com/AD1",
      "summary_html": "The cost and skill required to mount a serious cyberattack have collapsed, and most enterprise security programs still test on a quarterly or annual clock. In this episode, Sridhar Boddula, Head of Security Platform Engineering at MassMutual, breaks down why that mismatch is now the central risk for regulated enterprises and what has to change inside a security team to close it. He covers shifting from periodic testing to continuous validation, moving security from a gatekeeping function into the engineering pipeline, and the governance-first first step leaders should take before scaling any new tooling. This episode is sponsored by <a href=\"https://xbow.com/\">XBOW</a>. To learn how leading brands and AI startups connect with enterprise AI buyer audiences at scale, download our media kit at <a href=\"http://emerj.com/AD1\">emerj.com/AD1</a>",
